# What has to keep its line endings, whatever machine checks it out.
#
# This repository is written on Windows, where git hands files over with CRLF.
# A shell script with CRLF is a script whose every line ends in an invisible
# character: `#!/bin/sh\r` names a program that does not exist, and the error
# says so in a way nobody can read. A systemd unit is read the same way.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
